1
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:07,240
宇宙充满了壮观的景色
The Universe is full of breathtaking sights,

2
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:14,110
透过强大的望远镜
glimpsed through powerful telescopes.

3
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:17,080
然而我们究竟能否一游这些奇景
But will we ever travel to these places of wonder

4
00:00:17,190 --> 00:00:19,720
亲眼一睹它们呢？
and see them with our own eyes?

5
00:00:29,470 --> 00:00:33,100
现在科学家正在设计曲速引擎
Now scientists are designing warp drives,

6
00:00:33,210 --> 00:00:35,760
学习如何去撬开虫洞
learning how to pry open wormholes,

7
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:40,540
寻找宇宙结构上的缝隙
and looking for cracks in the fabric of the Cosmos.

8
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:46,140
为了将整个宇宙纳入我们的掌控之中
To bring the entire Universe within our grasp,

9
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:50,280
他们必须打破物理学的基本定律
they must break a fundamental law of physics.

10
00:00:50,390 --> 00:00:52,720
我们能够跑得比光还快么？
Can we travel faster than light?

11
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:58,730
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x08
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x08

12
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:04,100
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

13
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:10,840
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie Through the Wormhole.

14
00:01:14,890 --> 00:01:18,890
我们能够跑得比光还快么？
Can We Travel Faster Than Light?

15
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:26,180
人类一直在凝视群星
Humans have always gazed up at the stars.

16
00:01:26,290 --> 00:01:28,320
几千年来
For thousands of years,

17
00:01:28,430 --> 00:01:31,890
我们以为它们近如日月 -
we thought they were as close as the Sun and the Moon --

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,390
几乎近到触手可及
almost close enough to reach out and touch.

19
00:01:36,510 --> 00:01:41,230
但现在我们知道了宇宙有多浩瀚
But now we know just how vast the Universe is.

20
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:47,340
最近的恒星有约25万亿英里那么远
The closest star is about 25 trillion miles away.

21
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,770
我们今天最快的飞船
The fastest spacecraft we have today

22
00:01:49,890 --> 00:01:53,480
要花上1万多年才能到达那里
would take more than 10,000 years to get there.

23
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:56,750
要成为真正的宇宙公民
To become true citizens of the cosmos,

24
00:01:56,860 --> 00:02:01,250
我们就得做一些物理学宣称不可能的事情
we have to do something that physics says is impossible.

25
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:05,700
我们得跑得比光束还快
We have to travel faster than a beam of light.

26
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:13,400
小时候 我喜欢呆在密西西比的夜空下
As a child,l loved to be out under the Mississippi night sky,

27
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:15,870
在篝火旁取暖
warming myself by a campfire.

28
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:22,070
我会几个小时盯着舞动的火焰
l'd spend hours staring at the dancing flames.

29
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,540
这个火光究竟为何物？
What was this light made of?

30
00:02:24,650 --> 00:02:28,780
我困惑于它怎么会看似固体
l wondered how it could seem solid

31
00:02:28,890 --> 00:02:32,350
却又消失得无影无踪
but then vanish into nothingness.

32
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:53,070
肖恩.卡罗尔是一位理论物理学家
Sean Carroll is a theoretical physicist

33
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:56,270
来自加州理工学院
from the California lnstitute of Technology.

34
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:00,650
光的神秘属性让他思绪飞扬
The mysterious nature of light gets his mind racing.

35
00:03:03,460 --> 00:03:06,680
光的速度是每秒18.6万英里
The speed of light is 186,000 miles per second,

36
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:10,490
即每小时6.7亿英里
or 670 million miles per hour.

37
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:12,250
没有什么跑得比光速快
Nothing goes faster than the speed of light.

38
00:03:12,370 --> 00:03:14,020
那其实是宇宙间所有东西的
lt really is the maximum speed limit

39
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:15,460
最高限速
for everything in the Universe.

40
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:19,460
弗里曼：光速比音速要快百万倍
Light travels a million times faster than sound.

41
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:24,010
其速度之快 绕地球转7圈…
lt's fast enough to circle the Earth seven times...

42
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:27,640
…就一秒钟
...in just one second.

43
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:30,970
但是光的神秘之深奥
But the mystery of light

44
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:33,850
远超过其惊人的速度
goes much deeper than its breathtaking speed.

45
00:03:33,860 --> 00:03:36,550
其运动的方式不同于
The way it moves is different

46
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,180
宇宙间所有的东西
from everything else in the Universe.

47
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,720
卡罗尔：我们暂时要假装
We're gonna pretend for the moment

48
00:03:41,830 --> 00:03:44,020
我不是个守法公民
that l am not a respectable citizen

49
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:45,850
要乱抛垃圾了
and would do a little bit of littering.

50
00:03:45,970 --> 00:03:48,290
我们要加速我的车子
We're gonna add the velocity of my car,

51
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,990
这是30英里的时速
which is 30 miles an hour,

52
00:03:50,110 --> 00:03:51,660
如果我往同一个方向
and if l throw this Slurpee

53
00:03:51,770 --> 00:03:54,300
以20英里的时速抛出这个思乐冰
in the same direction at 20 miles an hour,

54
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:56,830
因为这是个司空见惯的日常事件
since this is an ordinary,everyday event,

55
00:03:56,950 --> 00:03:58,600
思乐冰的总速度
the total velocity of the Slurpee

56
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:01,270
实际上要达到每小时50英里了
is actually going to be 50 miles per hour.

57
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:10,410
如果我以30英里时速倒车
lf l'm going backwards at 30 miles an hour

58
00:04:10,530 --> 00:04:13,380
我以20英里时速抛出思乐冰
and l throw the Slurpee forward at 20,

59
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,520
路人会看到思乐冰
someone on the road will see the Slurpee

60
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:19,390
以10英里时速往后退去
move backwards at 10 miles an hour.

61
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:22,560
弗里曼：肖恩的车速
The speed of Sean's car

62
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:25,610
改变了他饮料的速度
changes the velocity of his beverage.

63
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:30,570
然而光并不遵守
But light doesn't abide by the same laws

64
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:33,240
支配冷饮的同样的规则
that govern cold drinks.

65
00:04:35,550 --> 00:04:37,670
我们车上射出一束光
When l push a beam of light out of the car,

66
00:04:37,790 --> 00:04:40,510
其总速度一直就是光的速度
the total velocity is always the speed of light.

67
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:44,210
光被视为以同样的速度在运动
Light would be seen to be moving at the same speed

68
00:04:44,330 --> 00:04:45,950
不管我的汽车在干嘛
no matter what my car was doing.

69
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,650
你不能将光速加在车速上
You don't add the speed of light to the speed of the car.

70
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,560
光速一直就是光速
The speed of light is always the speed of light.

71
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,990
弗里曼：光运动的这些奇怪的规则
These strange rules for how light moves

72
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:00,500
启迪了爱因斯坦
inspired Albert Einstein

73
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:03,370
重写了宇宙的基本定律
to rewrite the basic laws of the Universe.

74
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:07,940
他意识到空间与时间不是固定和绝对的
He realized that space and time were not fixed and absolute

75
00:05:08,050 --> 00:05:10,210
而是有联系和相对的
but connected and relevant.

76
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:11,510
一个想法
lt was an idea

77
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,780
引出了史上最著名的方程式 -
that led to the most famous equation in history --

78
00:05:14,890 --> 00:05:18,090
E等于MC的平方
"E" equals "MC" squared.

79
00:05:19,890 --> 00:05:21,280
卡罗尔：时间和空间
Time and space

80
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:23,220
实际上都属于一个基本的东西
are really part of one underlying thing

81
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:24,750
叫做时空
called space-time,

82
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:27,520
你如何把时空分割成时间与空间
and how you divide up space-time into time and space

83
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,320
取决于你如何运动
depends on how you're moving.

84
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,190
这样就有了各种推论
So there's various corollaries of that.

85
00:05:31,310 --> 00:05:34,030
一旦爱因斯坦认识到了时间与空间是一回事了
Once Einstein realized that time and space were the same thing,

86
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:36,830
他也就认识到了能量与质量是一回事了
he realized that energy and mass are the same thing.

87
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:39,670
弗里曼：E等于MC的平方
"E" equals "MC" squared

88
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:43,070
意味着你注入火箭的能量越多
implies that the more energy you inject into a rocket,

89
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,770
它所得到的质量就越大
the more mass it gains,

90
00:05:44,890 --> 00:05:48,640
也就越庞大 其加速也就越困难
and the more massive it is,the harder it is to accelerate.

91
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,650
将它提升到光速是不可能的
Boosting it to the speed of light is impossible

92
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:53,280
因为 在这个过程中
because,in the process,

93
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:57,420
火箭将会变得无比庞大
the rocket would become infinitely massive.

94
00:05:57,530 --> 00:05:59,290
它用来加速的能量
The energy it takes to accelerate

95
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,960
一再增加
increases and increases

96
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:03,490
才能让你逐步接近光速
as you come closer to the speed of light.

97
00:06:03,610 --> 00:06:06,730
原则上 你如果想跑到光速
lf,in principle,you wanted to go the speed of light,

98
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:08,800
你就需要无限的能量
you need an infinite amount of energy

99
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,230
来加速到那么快
to accelerate you that fast.

100
00:06:10,350 --> 00:06:11,970
亦即你会有越来越多的能量
Or you're gonna get more and more energy,

101
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:14,340
但是你不会得到更高的速度
but you're not going to get that much more speed.

102
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:20,390
弗里曼：相对论让光成为了我们的亦敌亦友
Relativity makes light both our friend and foe.

103
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:24,780
其巨大的速度让我们瞬间进行
lts tremendous speed lets us communicate

104
00:06:24,890 --> 00:06:29,120
地球上任意两点间的通讯
between any two points on Earth almost instantaneously.

105
00:06:29,230 --> 00:06:31,590
另一方面
On the other hand,

106
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:34,420
因为我们的速度永远都不能超过光
because we can never move faster than light,

107
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:36,660
我们就滞留在太阳系里了
we're stranded in the solar system,

108
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:39,670
恒星实在是遥不可及了
with the stars impossibly far away.

109
00:06:43,810 --> 00:06:49,200
此人认为他能够帮助我们逃离我们的宇宙牢狱
This man believes he can help us escape our cosmic prison.

110
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:53,440
他认为他找到了方法去弯曲爱因斯坦的规则
He think he's found a way to bend Einstein's rules

111
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:56,610
让我们去造访群星
and allow us to reach the stars.

112
00:06:56,730 --> 00:07:00,420
米给尔.阿库别瑞 墨西哥城里的物理学家
Miguel Alcubierre,a physicist in Mexico City,

113
00:07:00,530 --> 00:07:03,390
发明了曲速引擎
has invented the warp drive.

114
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,390
曲速引擎是一种从一地到另一地的方法
The warp drive is a way to get from one place to another

115
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,320
完全不同于我们通常所用的方法
that's very different from the way we normally do it.

116
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,560
通常 我们只是游走在空间里
So,normally we just move through space

117
00:07:09,670 --> 00:07:11,430
如走路 飞行等等
like we walk,or we fly,or whatever,

118
00:07:11,540 --> 00:07:13,660
然而曲速引擎 其想法是利用空间
but the warp drive,the idea is to use space,

119
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:15,660
让空间运动
to let space do the motion.

120
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:20,170
弗里曼：米给尔的想法源自
Miguel's idea stems from another aspect

121
00:07:20,280 --> 00:07:22,700
爱因斯坦相对论的另一面 -
of Einstein's theory of relativity --

122
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:27,220
即空间的形状可以被质量或能量所扭曲
that the shape of space can be distorted by mass or energy.

123
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:32,150
所以 基本思路是你扩张你身后的空间
So,the basic idea is you expand space behind you,

124
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:33,950
那实际上让你更进一步远离
which actually makes you even further away

125
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:35,150
你身后的那些物体
from those objects behind you,

126
00:07:35,260 --> 00:07:36,690
同时你压缩你前面的空间
and you contract space in front of you,

127
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,820
越来越接近你前面的物体
getting closer to the objects in front of you.

128
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:40,020
然而你根本就没动
But you don't move at all.

129
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:42,420
假设这是一艘飞船
Assume that this is a spaceship.

130
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:45,260
通常 你得飞越那样的空间
Normally,you would have to fly through space like that,

131
00:07:45,370 --> 00:07:47,660
你无法做到速度超过光速
and you cannot do this faster than the speed of light.

132
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:49,870
然而取而代之的是 让我们压缩这里的空间
But instead of that,let us contract space here

133
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:52,780
扩张这里 像这样
and expand it here,like this.

134
00:07:56,890 --> 00:07:58,310
这样 你看 现在这飞船
So,you see,now the spaceship

135
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:01,740
在逐步靠近这边而远离那边
is getting closer to this side and further away from that side.

136
00:08:01,860 --> 00:08:02,980
然而相对周围的物体
Bur it's actually not moving at all

137
00:08:03,090 --> 00:08:04,710
它其实根本就没动
with respect to the objects around it.

138
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:08,280
弗里曼：米给尔想法之美
The beauty of Miguel's idea

139
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:11,450
就在于飞船实际上
is that the spaceship actually stands still

140
00:08:11,570 --> 00:08:14,320
在时空泡里原地没动
inside the bubble of space-time.

141
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:18,190
因为它没动 所以它没有增加任何质量
Since it's not moving,it doesn't gain any mass.

142
00:08:18,310 --> 00:08:20,300
你实际上能够跑出任何速度
You can actually go at any speed,

143
00:08:20,410 --> 00:08:22,160
因为不存在物理学定律的限制
because there's no limit in the laws of physics

144
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:24,630
那就告诉你 你可以翘曲空间有多快
that tells you how fast you can warp space,

145
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:27,840
你可以扩张或压缩空间有多快
how fast you can expand or contract space.

146
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:31,010
你可以随心所欲达到任何速度
You can do it at any speed you want.

147
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:35,040
弗里曼：米给尔的曲速引擎是一个巧妙的方法
Miguel's warp drive is an ingenious way

148
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:38,350
绕开了爱因斯坦的宇宙速度极限
around Einstein's cosmic speed limit.

149
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:40,980
不过它还是理论上的
But it's still theoretical,

150
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:44,550
缺少一个关键的要素 -
and lacks one crucial ingredient --

151
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:47,820
一种奇怪的物质 叫做负能量
an ex otic substance called negative energy,

152
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:54,230
许多科学家甚至都无把握存在的东西
something that many scientists aren't even sure exists.

153
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:57,900
但是有一个人确信有负能量
But one man does believe in negative energy.

154
00:08:58,010 --> 00:09:01,910
他甚至声称他在自己的实验室里创造出来了
He even claims he's created it in his lab.

155
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,680
曲速引擎
The warp drive.

156
00:09:07,790 --> 00:09:10,510
听起来好像是科幻
lt sounds like science fiction,

157
00:09:10,630 --> 00:09:13,980
但在翘曲的空间泡泡中穿行在
but the idea of surfing across the Universe

158
00:09:14,100 --> 00:09:16,450
整个宇宙间的想法
in a warping bubble of space

159
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:20,720
对爱因斯坦来说完全说得通
would make perfect sense to Einstein.

160
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:23,260
有一个障碍
There is one snag.

161
00:09:23,370 --> 00:09:25,460
曲速引擎只能靠
A warp drive can only function

162
00:09:25,570 --> 00:09:27,930
一个神秘的能源来运作 -
with a mysterious power source --

163
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:29,730
负能量
negative energy.

164
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:33,600
如今 大多数科学家认为负能量
And today,most scientists believe negative energy

165
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:36,680
只是一个未经证实的理论性概念
is just an unproven theoretical concept.

166
00:09:41,020 --> 00:09:45,280
然而 斯蒂夫.拉蒙诺 耶鲁大学的原子物理学家
But Steve Lamoreaux,an atomic physicist at Yale University,

167
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:50,250
他立志要追查出此种奇怪的能量
has made it his mission to track down this ex otic form of energy,

168
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:53,390
他认为答案就在我们身边
and he believes the answer is all around us

169
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,730
在空间本身的构造中
in the fabric of space itself.

170
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,530
我们通常将真空的空间
We normally think of the vacuum of space

171
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,860
看作是空无一物
as being completely empty,

172
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:05,730
然而事实上 真空中有能量密度
but,in fact,there is energy density in empty space,

173
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:08,210
我们将其称之为空间的零点能
and we call that the zero-point energy of space.

174
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:12,610
弗里曼：量子力学说
The theory of quantum mechanics

175
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:15,840
预言真空空间其实始终是波光粼粼
predicts that empty space is actually constantly shimmering

176
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:18,380
那是现实中此起彼落的粒子
with microscopic pulses of energy

177
00:10:18,490 --> 00:10:21,550
所产生的微量能量脉冲
as particles pop in and out of existence.

178
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,250
为了产生负能量
To make negative energy,

179
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:27,190
你就得找到方法去抑制此种无休无止的震颤
you have to find a way to suppress this constant chatter.

180
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:30,390
斯蒂夫意识到要做到这一点的方法
Steve realized the way to do this

181
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:33,340
就在于改变空间的形态
was to change the shape of space.

182
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:38,000
拉蒙诺：有一个很好的比喻
There's a nice analogy.

183
00:10:38,110 --> 00:10:41,870
你如果有两条船在狂涛骇浪之中
lf you have two ships on a rough ocean,

184
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:45,440
一条船就会反射出它所产生的波浪
one ship will kind of reflect waves from it.

185
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:47,540
另一条也会做同样的事情
The other one does the same thing.

186
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:50,510
两条船之间的波浪密度相对
So the wave density between the two ships is a little bit less

187
00:10:50,630 --> 00:10:53,450
一条船置身于波浪中要小一点
compared to one by itself which is surrounded by a rough sea.

188
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:56,420
所以说 你将两条船放在波浪之中
So,you put two ships on a rough sea,

189
00:10:56,530 --> 00:10:59,620
它们会相互吸引 走到一起
they'll be mutually attracted,and they'll come together.

190
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:01,720
弗里曼：斯蒂夫推断如果他在真空中
Steve reasoned that if he created

191
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,760
创造出一个足够窄的地带
a narrow-enough region of empty space

192
00:11:03,870 --> 00:11:05,890
如这两条船之间的区域
like the area between the two ships,

193
00:11:06,010 --> 00:11:08,800
那么某些波光粼粼的零点能
then some of the shimmering zero-point energy

194
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:10,670
就不会在里头了
would not fit inside it.

195
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:14,270
狭窄地带外面的真空能量
The energy of empty space outside the narrow region

196
00:11:14,380 --> 00:11:17,540
会较为强大 迫使其收缩
would be stronger and force it to shrink.

197
00:11:17,650 --> 00:11:22,140
那个力量就是负能量的标记
That force would be the signature of negative energy,

198
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:26,750
斯蒂夫着手在其实验室里创造它
and Steve set out to create it in his lab.

199
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:30,050
就是这个想法消耗了
lt was an idea that would consume him

200
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:33,220
他十余年光阴
for more than a decade.

201
00:11:33,330 --> 00:11:34,790
我们称这个实验为“时间机器”
We call the experiment "The Time Machine."

202
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:35,990
眼下是时间机器2
Actually,the "Time Machine 2."

203
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,830
这是实验的第二版
This is the second version of the experiment.

204
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:41,310
我们这样说是因为我的15年人生
We call it that because l invested 15 years of my life

205
00:11:41,420 --> 00:11:42,420
投入到了这个实验里了
in this measurement.

206
00:11:42,530 --> 00:11:43,770
大量的时间
That's a lot of time.

207
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:47,000
所以 它是费时机器 更准确地说吧
So,it's a time-wasting machine,more accurately defined.

208
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:51,270
弗里曼：这个真空室里
lnside this vacuum chamber

209
00:11:51,390 --> 00:11:52,910
放有两块小金属板
are two small metal plates

210
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,210
彼此相距不超过
sitting less than the width of a human hair

211
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,850
人的头发的宽度
apart from one another.

212
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,220
为了让它们如此接近又不触及
To get them that close and not touch,

213
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:02,250
金属板得非常平滑
the metal has to be perfectly flat,

214
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:05,090
几乎达到原子级别
down almost to the atomic level.

215
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:10,530
自由空间里的零点波动
The zero-point fluctuations of free space

216
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:12,590
不会就发生在这些板子之间
won't fit between those plates,as well,

217
00:12:12,710 --> 00:12:14,700
因此当你把两块板子放在一起时
so when you bring these two plates together,

218
00:12:14,810 --> 00:12:16,770
板子之间的波动会小于
there are fewer fluctuations between the plates

219
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,030
板子外面的波动
than there are outside the plates.

220
00:12:18,150 --> 00:12:19,470
力在积累
The force builds up,

221
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:21,440
实际上是随着板子的逐步靠近
and it actually gets stronger and stronger

222
00:12:21,550 --> 00:12:23,370
变得越来越强
as the plates get closer together,

223
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:27,280
我们所说的力就是产生于负能量
and that force we refer to as arising from negative energy.

224
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:31,710
弗里曼：板子外面的零点能的波动
The zero-point energy fluctuations outside the plates

225
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:33,780
要强于板子之间的波动
are stronger than those between,

226
00:12:33,900 --> 00:12:37,690
因此外部的压力会将它们推在一起
so pressure from the outside pushes them together.

227
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:40,260
或者换个角度来思考一下
Or think of it another way.

228
00:12:40,370 --> 00:12:45,330
板子之间的负能量扩张了其周围的空间
The negative energy between the plates expands space around it.

229
00:12:49,080 --> 00:12:52,500
斯蒂夫多年一丝不苟的工作
Steve's years of meticulous labor

230
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:54,800
已经使其成为了地球上第一人
have made him the first person on Earth

231
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,870
测量到了负能量所产生的力道
to have measured a force produced by negative energy.

232
00:12:57,990 --> 00:13:01,510
但是他所测到的量微乎其微
But the amount he has detected is minuscule.

233
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,610
该力相当于一个红血球
The force is equal to the weight of a red blood cell

234
00:13:06,730 --> 00:13:09,720
在地球重力场里的重量 所以极其微弱
in the Earth's gravitational field,so it's tiny.

235
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,790
但你若是累积上数千块这样的板子
But if you add up thousands of these plates

236
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,060
就像我们实验里的这些
like we have in our experiment,

237
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:17,590
你就能获得明显而有效地力道
you can actually achieve a palpable and useful force.

238
00:13:17,710 --> 00:13:19,760
弗里曼：斯蒂夫的发现
Steve's discovery

239
00:13:19,870 --> 00:13:23,370
有可能只是朝向曲速引擎的起步
may only be a baby step towards warp drive,

240
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:25,070
然而他证明了
but he's confirmed

241
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:28,470
米给尔.阿库别瑞的曲速引擎理论
that Miguel Alcubierre's warp drive theory

242
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:31,180
并不违背物理定律
does not violate the laws of physics.

243
00:13:36,490 --> 00:13:41,480
弯曲空间及推动曲速引擎所需的能量
The energy needed to warp space and propel a warp drive forward

244
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:44,020
确实存在着
actually exists.

245
00:13:44,130 --> 00:13:48,160
然而他也打开了其他东西的大门 -
But he's also opened the door to something else --

246
00:13:48,270 --> 00:13:53,670
虫洞 空间自身结构的裂口
the wormhole,a rip in the fabric of space itself.

247
00:13:55,410 --> 00:13:58,700
如果这一理论对象存在
lf this theoretical object exists,

248
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:01,100
那么你就可以在一个地方进去
you could enter it in one place

249
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:05,310
稍后现身 穿越了整个星系
and emerge moments later clear across the galaxy.

250
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:10,350
然而虫洞不止是科幻么？
But are wormholes more than a science-fiction fantasy?

251
00:14:10,460 --> 00:14:15,050
若是这样 我们如何知道它们会将我们带去何方呢？
And,if so,how would we know where they would take us?

252
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:20,890
现在有位物理学家大胆闯入了这些奇怪的大门
Now one physicist is daring to enter these strange portals

253
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:24,600
谋划穿越虫洞
and plot a course through the wormhole.

254
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,130
我们都听说过虫洞
We've all heard of wormholes.

255
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,970
它们是宇宙捷径
They're cosmic shortcuts

256
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:36,370
将外星世界几乎就放在了我们的家门口
that put alien worlds practically on our doorstep.

257
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:39,570
但是我们如何真正构建出一个来呢？
But how would we actually build one?

258
00:14:39,690 --> 00:14:42,310
我们如何去利用它呢？
And how would we use one?

259
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:47,280
通过虫洞旅行需要异乎寻常的技术
Travel by wormhole requires ex otic technology

260
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:52,460
以及闯入未知世界的勇气
and the courage to jump into the unknown.

261
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:02,760
我们的星球布满了各种通道
Our planet is riddled with passageways.

262
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:07,540
我们经常会走过坚固的隧道
We regularly travel through strong,stable tunnels

263
00:15:07,650 --> 00:15:10,010
直穿大山
cut through massive mountains.

264
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:16,040
现在我们进入了一条漂亮坚固的隧道
Well,here we're entering a nice,solid tunnel.

265
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:19,350
它的构造 看上去是钢筋混凝土
lt's made of -- looks like concrete and reinforced steel.

266
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,280
很坚固
Very solid.

267
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,490
一个可靠地运输手段
A reliable means of transportation.

268
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,990
我驾车驶入 我马上要出去了
l drive my car in. l'm gonna come out.

269
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:29,090
我随时都知道情况
l know what's happening at all times.

270
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:32,960
弗里曼：物理学家斯蒂芬.舒沉迷于
Physicist Steven Shu is fascinated by the concepts

271
00:15:33,070 --> 00:15:35,360
稳定与不稳定说
of stability and instability,

272
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,010
它们在股市里…
be they in the stock market...

273
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:38,120
抛
Sell.

274
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,500
…在房地产价值里…
...in real-estate values...

275
00:15:39,610 --> 00:15:40,670
长线
Long.

276
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:44,110
…或是在时空虫洞里
...or in space-time wormholes.

277
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,640
舒：我们观察一个特定系统时
One of the fundamental properties

278
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:48,340
在物理学上所观察的基本属性之一
that we look at in physics when we look at a particular system

279
00:15:48,460 --> 00:15:51,880
就是该系统是稳定的还是不稳定的
is whether that system is stable or unstable.

280
00:15:51,990 --> 00:15:55,380
例子就是这支笔 它像这样是稳定的
An example would be a pen which is balanced like this.

281
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,920
它可能没事 此时它完全平衡
lt might be okay when it's exactly balanced,

282
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,990
但哪怕是轻微的碰撞都会使其
but even a slight bump will send it

283
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:02,420
进入截然不同的状态
into a drastically different state.

284
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:05,360
我们决定观察是否能构建一个虫洞
We decided to look at whether one could build a wormhole

285
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:07,230
它具有良好的特性
that had nice properties

286
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:11,160
比如其动作是可预见性的 是稳定的
such as its behavior is predictable and it's stable.

287
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:12,270
那是两个标准
Those are two criteria

288
00:16:12,390 --> 00:16:14,070
使你能拥有真正的虫洞
you'd like to have for a real wormhole.

289
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:16,540
弗里曼：构建虫洞的规则
The rules of building wormholes

290
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:19,370
出自爱因斯坦的相对论
start with Einstein's theory of relativity,

291
00:16:19,490 --> 00:16:22,840
它告诉你如何去弯曲和塑造空间
which tells you how to bend and shape space

292
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:26,250
仿佛它是块柔软的床单
as if it were a flexible sheet.

293
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:28,020
试想这张纸
lmagine this sheet of paper,

294
00:16:28,130 --> 00:16:31,220
试想你是生活在这张纸上的一只蚂蚁
and imagine that you're an ant living on this sheet of paper.

295
00:16:31,330 --> 00:16:33,620
如果你想从这一点走到这一点
lf you want to travel from this point to this point,

296
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:36,760
你可能得从这里一直走到这里
you might have to walk all the way from here to here.

297
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:41,530
但如果这张纸弯曲了 所绕的路
But if the paper were curved,the long way around

298
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:45,330
就会涉及到像这样一直要绕过这张纸
would involve walking all the way around the paper like this.

299
00:16:45,450 --> 00:16:47,740
不过你可以设想有一个小管道
But you can imagine that there would be a little Tube

300
00:16:47,850 --> 00:16:50,100
将这一点直接连到这一点
connecting this point directly to this point,

301
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:52,870
蚂蚁就可以穿过去了
and the ant could just slip through.

302
00:16:52,990 --> 00:16:56,210
科幻中的虫洞
Wormholes in science fiction

303
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:59,950
敞开了入口让星舰驶入
have gaping entrances that a starship can dive into.

304
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:05,050
不过那些二维的描绘
But those two-dimensional renderings

305
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:08,970
粉饰了虫洞真实的结构
gloss over the true architecture of wormholes.

306
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:12,860
在这个二维的比喻中
ln this two-dimensional analogy,

307
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:16,700
管子的开口仅仅是个圆圈
the opening of the straw is just a circle.

308
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:18,930
但因为我们生活在三维里
But,because we live in three dimensions,

309
00:17:19,050 --> 00:17:20,240
虫洞的开口
the opening of the wormhole

310
00:17:20,350 --> 00:17:23,340
实际上会是在泡泡的里面
would actually be like the interior of a bubble.

311
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:30,510
弗里曼：这就是
This is what the mouth

312
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:32,580
真实虫洞口可能的模样
of a real wormhole might look like

313
00:17:32,690 --> 00:17:36,820
如果它们蛰伏在空间某个地方的话
if they are lurking somewhere out there in space.

314
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,120
不过斯蒂芬在琢磨
But Steven wondered

315
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:41,600
我们是否有可能从头开始构建我们自己的虫洞
if we might be able to build our own from scratch.

316
00:17:45,670 --> 00:17:49,400
宇宙工程师首先要创造两个口子
A cosmic engineer would first create two mouths

317
00:17:49,510 --> 00:17:51,930
并将它们联系起来
and connect them.

318
00:17:52,050 --> 00:17:55,670
然后 他将其中的一个口子拉至数光年外 -
Then,he would drag one of the mouths light-years away --

319
00:17:55,780 --> 00:18:00,310
但是两个口子之间的管道并不属于我们空间
but the tunnel between the two mouths is not part of our space

320
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:02,740
可以保持得很短
and could remain very short.

321
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,350
这是个很简单的想法
lt's a simple idea,

322
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:06,910
但是防止虫洞口子及隧道的垮塌
but the vast amount of negative energy

323
00:18:07,030 --> 00:18:10,820
所需的大量的负能量
needed to keep the wormhole's mouth and tunnel from collapsing

324
00:18:10,930 --> 00:18:14,060
却是一个难以控制的东西
is tricky stuff to control.

325
00:18:14,170 --> 00:18:16,620
稳定虫洞极具挑战
lt's very challenging to stabilize a wormhole.

326
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:21,430
所有的虫洞 根据我们从广义相对论的理解
All wormholes,as far as we know from general relativity,

327
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:25,000
都需要这种特殊负能量的奇异物质
require this kind of special negative energy ex otic matter.

328
00:18:25,110 --> 00:18:29,540
问题在于该物质是否能够稳定
The question is whether that matter itself can be stable.

329
00:18:29,650 --> 00:18:34,010
弗里曼：斯蒂芬计算了负能量
Steven crunched the numbers on how negative energy

330
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:37,780
如何在虫洞边缘与正常的物质发生反应
would react with normal matter on the fringes of the wormhole

331
00:18:37,890 --> 00:18:41,550
来探索它们能否和平共处
to discover whether they could coexist in a stable way.

332
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:45,500
舒：我们的计算证明它们是不稳定的
And we've proven mathematically they're unstable.

333
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:51,090
那将是使用十分危险的装置
That would be a very dangerous device to use,

334
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:52,930
因为你一旦稍稍碰撞它
because once you bump it a little bit,

335
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:56,060
整个装置就会土崩瓦解
the entire device could just fall apart.

336
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,700
如果我试图进入一个不稳定的虫洞
lf l try to get into an unstable wormhole,

337
00:18:58,810 --> 00:19:00,870
就好像试图将我的手指伸进这个泡泡中
it's like trying to put my finger into this bubble.

338
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,900
它就会破裂
lt'll just pop.

339
00:19:03,020 --> 00:19:05,910
弗里曼：保持虫洞打开所需的负能量
The negative energy needed to keep a wormhole open

340
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:08,340
天生就是极不稳定的
is inherently too unstable.

341
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:10,750
人造虫洞在人们试图踏足其中时
A man-made wormhole would collapse

342
00:19:10,860 --> 00:19:14,420
瞬间就会垮塌
the instant someone tries to step inside.

343
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:16,620
但或许有另一个方法
But there might be another way.

344
00:19:16,730 --> 00:19:21,220
并不是靠利用我们自己构建的宇宙捷径
Not by using cosmic shortcuts that we have built ourselves,

345
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:23,290
而是靠搜索有可能隐藏在我们周围的
but by searching for microscopic ones

346
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:26,060
微型虫洞
that could be hiding all around us.

347
00:19:26,170 --> 00:19:27,360
就如真空中
Just as empty space

348
00:19:27,480 --> 00:19:30,300
充满了微型能量脉冲一样
is fizzing with microscopic pulses of energy,

349
00:19:30,410 --> 00:19:31,770
有些理论家认为
some theorists believe

350
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:35,370
它也可能布满了微型孔洞
it could also be riddled with microscopic holes.

351
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,870
量子虫洞有可能
There could be quantum wormholes

352
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,910
就是大爆炸遗留下来的
that are just left over from the Big Bang,

353
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,780
或者就在很近很近处
or at very,very short distances,

354
00:19:40,890 --> 00:19:42,680
你可能会有一点小小的波动
you could have little fluctuations

355
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:45,750
这样时空就以一种有趣的方式将其自身连接起来
where space-time just connects to itself in a funny way,

356
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,780
那就是量子虫洞
and that would be a quantum wormhole.

357
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,550
如果它们刚好碰上一点波动
lf they just happened as a little fluctuation,

358
00:19:49,660 --> 00:19:53,620
那将是极其微小的 大概一米的10的负25次方
they would be incredibly tiny,like 10 to the minus-35 meters.

359
00:19:53,730 --> 00:19:57,190
弗里曼：微型量子虫洞
Microscopic quantum wormholes

360
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,290
是空间的量子波动
are quantum fluctuations in space

361
00:19:59,410 --> 00:20:04,500
始终不断地冒出 湮灭 再冒出
that perpetually appear,disappear,and reappear again.

362
00:20:04,610 --> 00:20:07,240
由于我们不必去构建其入口
Since we don't have to construct their portals,

363
00:20:07,350 --> 00:20:11,670
斯蒂芬觉得它们或许可以安全进入
Steven suspects they might be safe to enter.

364
00:20:11,790 --> 00:20:17,750
但是在你试图跳进去之前 已经意识到暗藏杀机
But before you try jumping into one,be aware there's a catch.

365
00:20:17,860 --> 00:20:20,750
舒：量子力学的东西时说不准的
Quantum mechanical things are fuzzy.

366
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:23,120
它们本质上是随机和不可预见的
They're intrinsically random and unpredictable.

367
00:20:23,230 --> 00:20:24,750
因此如果我们进入了一个量子虫洞
So if we were in a quantum wormhole,

368
00:20:24,870 --> 00:20:26,290
我们有可能被搞得不知天南地北
we might be shaken around,

369
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,160
我们会无法确定我们出去是哪里
and we wouldn't quite know where we're gonna come out.

370
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:30,960
你不会希望进入了一个隧道
You wouldn't want to get into a tunnel

371
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:33,160
有可能终点是太平洋的海底
that might end in the bottom of the pacific ocean

372
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:35,560
或者是你不想呆在上面的山顶
or on a mountaintop that you didn't want to be on.

373
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:39,930
弗里曼：量子虫洞无法估计抵达的时间
Quantum wormholes have no estimated times of arrival,

374
00:20:40,050 --> 00:20:43,450
你的目的地是未知的
and your destination is unknown.

375
00:20:46,650 --> 00:20:50,880
你最终结束有可能是任何地方
You could end up anywhere

376
00:20:50,990 --> 00:20:52,720
或任何时候
or anywhen.

377
00:21:02,340 --> 00:21:05,030
超越光速穿越虫洞
Traveling faster than light through a wormhole

378
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:07,030
会是一个冒险的举动
would be a risky ride.

379
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:10,360
你得赌上一把了
You've got to be willing to roll the dice.

380
00:21:10,480 --> 00:21:15,800
不过对谨慎的旅客可能会有更安全的方法
But there may be a safer way for the cautious traveler.

381
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:20,140
试想一下能够从这里移动到那里
lmagine being able to move from here to there

382
00:21:20,250 --> 00:21:23,450
完全不用挪动
without ever moving at all.

383
00:21:26,160 --> 00:21:31,590
好 人类首次出游星际貌似漫漫长路
Well,Mankind's first journey to the stars looks a long way off.

384
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:35,490
我们至少在几个世纪里不会掌握
We won't master the technology of wormholes and warp drives

385
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,860
虫洞及曲速引擎的技术
for centuries at least.

386
00:21:37,970 --> 00:21:41,630
不过有另一个方法去穿梭宇宙
But there's another way to zip around the cosmos.

387
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:45,170
我们可以将我们的躯体变成信息
We could turn our bodies into information

388
00:21:45,280 --> 00:21:49,870
将那信息以光速
and send that information from place to place

389
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:52,480
从一地发送至另一地
at the speed of light.

390
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:57,580
克里斯.门罗和史蒂夫.奥尔莫斯琴科
Chris Monroe and Steve Olmschenk

391
00:21:57,690 --> 00:22:01,480
是马里兰大学的量子物理学家
are quantum physicists at the University of Maryland.

392
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:04,720
他们是隐形传送的开拓者
They are pioneers of teleportation.

393
00:22:04,830 --> 00:22:07,460
他们的工作就是要在两个不同地点
Their work is all about making connections

394
00:22:07,570 --> 00:22:10,630
所发生的事件之间建立联系 -
between events taking place in two separate locations --

395
00:22:10,740 --> 00:22:15,440
这些事件通常没有任何联系
events which normally have no connection whatsoever.

396
00:22:17,880 --> 00:22:21,440
我们要用硬币来演示一个简单的实验
We're gonna demonstrate a simple experiment using standard coins

397
00:22:21,550 --> 00:22:23,700
来看看单枚硬币的随机性
just to show the randomness of the individual coins

398
00:22:23,820 --> 00:22:26,450
以及两枚硬币之间的随机性
and the randomness between the two coins.

399
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,560
好嘞
All right.

400
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,980
抛
Flip.

401
00:22:30,090 --> 00:22:31,890
正面 背面
-- Heads. -- Tails.

402
00:22:34,500 --> 00:22:36,050
背面 背面
-- Tails. -- Tails.

403
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:38,420
你可以看到 用两枚硬币
So,as you can see,with two regular coins,

404
00:22:38,530 --> 00:22:41,920
我们就能够得到彼此之间的整个随机结果
we get completely random results between each other.

405
00:22:42,040 --> 00:22:43,460
弗里曼：如果克里斯和史蒂夫
lf Chris and Steve

406
00:22:43,570 --> 00:22:46,530
能够让两枚硬币以同样的方式抛下
could make the two coins always land the same way,

407
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,430
那么他们就将成功地
then they would have succeeded

408
00:22:48,540 --> 00:22:52,730
把硬币上的信息 - 正面或背面 -
in teleporting the information on the coin -- heads or tails --

409
00:22:52,850 --> 00:22:54,900
从一地传送到另一地
from one place to the other.

410
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:58,940
他们有一个想法就是如何去做到这一点
And they had an idea of just how to do this.

411
00:22:59,050 --> 00:23:02,180
他们会用到量子纠缠
They would use quantum entanglement,

412
00:23:02,290 --> 00:23:04,710
一个能够在微观物体之间
a strange effect that can create a link

413
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:07,260
建立起联系的奇怪结果
between microscopic objects.

414
00:23:11,670 --> 00:23:13,550
炸弹爆炸时
When a bomb explodes

415
00:23:13,670 --> 00:23:16,360
两块弹片飞出
and two pieces of shrapnel come flying out,

416
00:23:16,470 --> 00:23:20,800
每一块都是独自行动 不受别人的影响
each one moves independently and is unaffected by the other.

417
00:23:20,910 --> 00:23:24,470
现在来想象一下亚原子世界里的炸弹
Now imagine a bomb in a subatomic world.

418
00:23:24,580 --> 00:23:27,030
两颗粒子弹片飞出
Two particles of shrapnel fly out,

419
00:23:27,150 --> 00:23:29,540
然而此时 量子纠缠
but this time,quantum entanglement

420
00:23:29,650 --> 00:23:31,410
意味着一片运动的方式
means the way one moves

421
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:34,240
完全依赖于别人
is entirely dependent on the other.

422
00:23:34,350 --> 00:23:36,510
如果一片是顺时针旋转
lf one piece is spinning clockwise,

423
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:38,650
你可以推断另一片的动作
you can deduce that the other piece

424
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:41,520
是逆时针的移动的
is moving counterclockwise.

425
00:23:41,630 --> 00:23:44,720
如果史蒂夫和克里斯的硬币是纠缠的
lf Steve and Chris' coins were entangled,

426
00:23:44,830 --> 00:23:49,160
每当史蒂夫抛出正面 克里斯则抛出背面
whenever Steve tosses heads,Chris will toss tails.

427
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:53,790
如果史蒂夫抛出背面 克里斯则抛出正面
lf Steve tosses tails,Chris will toss heads.

428
00:23:53,910 --> 00:23:55,530
背面 正面
-- Tails. -- Heads.

429
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:59,370
因此 即使抛出的硬币的一面完全是随机的
So,even though the coin flip on one side is completely random,

430
00:23:59,480 --> 00:24:01,700
但两枚硬币之间存在着联系
there are correlations between the two coins,

431
00:24:01,820 --> 00:24:04,680
这就是纠缠的标准特征
and this is the defining feature of entanglement.

432
00:24:06,090 --> 00:24:09,340
弗里曼：物理学家一直致力利用纠缠
Physicists have been struggling to use entanglement

433
00:24:09,460 --> 00:24:13,210
在两地之间传送物质已有20多个年头了
to teleport matter from place to place for more than two decades.

434
00:24:13,330 --> 00:24:17,280
史蒂夫和克里斯是首个成功者
Steve and Chris are the first to succeed.

435
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:22,890
他们从一种叫做镱的元素的两个原子着手
They begin with two atoms of an element called ytterbium.

436
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:25,390
其实验是 我们从两束的原子着手
The experiment is,we start with two trapped atoms

437
00:24:25,510 --> 00:24:27,060
它们彼此隔着桌子
that are across the table from each other.

438
00:24:27,170 --> 00:24:29,560
门罗：这些原子用磁场悬浮着
These atoms are sort of levitated with fields,

439
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:30,930
如磁悬浮列车那样
like a levitated train.

440
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:33,100
它们放置于真空室里 没有东西碰及它们
They're in a vacuum chamber,so nothing touches them.

441
00:24:33,210 --> 00:24:34,970
它们几乎完全 -
They're almost complete--

442
00:24:35,080 --> 00:24:38,170
它们几乎就是你所能得到的完美的隔离
they're as close as you can get to perfect isolation.

443
00:24:38,290 --> 00:24:41,010
弗里曼：史蒂夫和克里斯
Steve and Chris

444
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:44,410
利用微波辐射将所谓的量子位的量子信息
write quantum information called qubits

445
00:24:44,530 --> 00:24:47,820
写入了第一个原子
into the first atom using microwave radiation.

446
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:51,750
量子位成了原子的正面或背面
The qubits become the atoms' heads or tails.

447
00:24:51,870 --> 00:24:53,420
接下来 我们用这束快速脉冲光束
Then,we excite both atoms

448
00:24:53,530 --> 00:24:55,020
来激发这两个原子
with this fast pulse of light,

449
00:24:55,140 --> 00:24:56,220
如果我们所做的是正确的话
and if we do it right,

450
00:24:56,340 --> 00:24:57,890
我们就能确保光子
we can make sure that the photon

451
00:24:58,010 --> 00:25:00,730
与原子的内部状态纠缠在一起
is then entangled with the internal state of the atom.

452
00:25:00,850 --> 00:25:03,600
光子变成了使者
The photons become the messengers,

453
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:06,700
携带着原子的信息穿越了实验室
carrying the atoms' information across the lab.

454
00:25:06,810 --> 00:25:09,100
克里斯和史蒂夫将每个原子发出的光子
Chris and Steve aim the photon

455
00:25:09,220 --> 00:25:12,270
瞄准同一个目标
from each atom at the same target.

456
00:25:12,390 --> 00:25:14,840
当它们相遇时 就会纠缠在一起
When they meet,they become entangled,

457
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:19,480
从而将发出它们的两个原子纠缠了起来
which,in turn,entangles the two atoms they came from.

458
00:25:19,590 --> 00:25:20,680
它们无论如何不会相互靠拢
They've been nowhere near each other,

459
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:21,950
它们永远都碰不到一起
they've never seen each other,

460
00:25:22,060 --> 00:25:23,120
但现在这两个原子
but now these two atoms

461
00:25:23,230 --> 00:25:24,850
它们彼此隔着桌子
which are across the table from each other

462
00:25:24,970 --> 00:25:26,150
现在纠缠在了一起
are now entangled,

463
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:28,220
它们以某种方式分享着我们一开始
and they somehow share the information

464
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:29,960
写入第一个原子里的信息
that we first wrote into the first atom.

465
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:31,760
那就是所谓的量子隐形传送
That's called quantum teleportation,

466
00:25:31,870 --> 00:25:34,030
因为信息 在某种意义上
because the information,in a sense,

467
00:25:34,140 --> 00:25:35,300
是决不会旅行的
never really made the trip.

468
00:25:35,410 --> 00:25:37,360
决不存在任何物理作用
There was never really any physical interaction.

469
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:39,730
那全在于这种神奇的纠缠
lt's all because of this magic of entanglement

470
00:25:39,850 --> 00:25:41,440
让我们做到了这个
that allows us to do that.

471
00:25:41,550 --> 00:25:44,970
我认为爱因斯坦用了最恰当的话来描述它
And l think Einstein had the best words to describe it.

472
00:25:45,090 --> 00:25:47,820
他称纠缠为远距离的幽灵行动
He called entanglement "Spooky action at a distance."

473
00:25:50,060 --> 00:25:53,010
弗里曼：史蒂夫和克里斯成功地
Steve and Chris have successfully transferred

474
00:25:53,130 --> 00:25:55,950
将信息从一个原子传送到另一个原子
the information from one atom to the other.

475
00:25:56,060 --> 00:26:00,090
也就是说 他们传送了原子
ln other words,they teleported the atom.

476
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:04,360
这是首次有人以光速
lt's the first time anyone has ever beamed matter across space

477
00:26:04,470 --> 00:26:06,590
隔空传送物质
at the speed of light.

478
00:26:06,710 --> 00:26:08,300
他们已经在着手
And they're already working

479
00:26:08,410 --> 00:26:11,630
更加雄心勃勃的隐形传送实验
on more ambitious teleportation experiments.

480
00:26:11,750 --> 00:26:13,330
门罗：不过好消息是
But the good news is,

481
00:26:13,450 --> 00:26:17,710
想法是用比单个原子复杂的东西来研究 -
this idea works with matter more complex than a single atom --

482
00:26:17,820 --> 00:26:19,670
比方说 几百个原子
say,a few hundred atoms.

483
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:22,840
弗里曼：几百个原子会取得进展的
A few hundred atoms would be progress,

484
00:26:22,960 --> 00:26:24,510
但真正的问题在于
but the real question

485
00:26:24,630 --> 00:26:27,550
我们是否能够完整地传送
is whether we will ever be able to teleport the state

486
00:26:27,660 --> 00:26:30,820
整个人体的7000万亿万亿个原子
of all the 7,000 trillion trillion atoms

487
00:26:30,930 --> 00:26:34,290
从一地到另外一地
in an entire person from one place to another

488
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:40,060
转换成一堆有机物体从而复制你我
to turn a pile of organic matter into a copy of you or me.

489
00:26:40,170 --> 00:26:41,800
那是个苛刻的要求
lt's a tall order.

490
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:45,170
我们这里有个樱桃馅饼
Well,we have a cherry pie,

491
00:26:45,280 --> 00:26:49,140
馅饼有个特定的形态
and the pie is in a particular state.

492
00:26:49,250 --> 00:26:52,840
所有的原子 大多是碳和有机分子
All the atoms,mostly carbon and organic molecules,

493
00:26:52,950 --> 00:26:54,110
做成了这个馅饼
make up this pie,

494
00:26:54,220 --> 00:26:55,880
不过它们明显的状态
but they're obviously in a state

495
00:26:55,990 --> 00:26:58,010
我们都承认其为樱桃馅饼
that we all recognize as a cherry pie.

496
00:26:58,130 --> 00:26:59,210
样子很好看
Looks pretty good.

497
00:26:59,330 --> 00:27:01,550
弗里曼：为了让克里斯
ln order for Chris

498
00:27:01,660 --> 00:27:03,980
隐形传送樱桃馅饼里的原子
to teleport the atoms inside the cherry pie,

499
00:27:04,100 --> 00:27:07,590
他需要采集其中每一个原子的信息
he needs to gather information about every single one of them,

500
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:10,670
这有点混乱
which gets a little messy.

501
00:27:18,050 --> 00:27:21,000
这里所有的原子都代表着樱桃馅饼
All the atoms in here are representative of a cherry pie,

502
00:27:21,110 --> 00:27:23,100
但肯定看上去不像是樱桃馅饼
but it certainly doesn't look like a cherry pie,

503
00:27:23,220 --> 00:27:24,610
其原因就在于原子的
and the reason is the atoms aren't arranged

504
00:27:24,720 --> 00:27:25,840
排列方法不对
in the right way.

505
00:27:25,950 --> 00:27:28,880
这个烤盘里约有10的27次方个原子
They are about 10 to the 27 atoms in this tin.

506
00:27:28,990 --> 00:27:31,280
那可是万亿万亿万亿个原子啊
That's a billion billion billion atoms.

507
00:27:31,390 --> 00:27:33,280
要顾及的可能性的量
Consider the number of possibilities

508
00:27:33,390 --> 00:27:36,420
那是万亿万亿万亿个原子的排列
that a billion billion billion atoms can be arranged.

509
00:27:36,530 --> 00:27:39,320
那个数字简直不可理喻
lt's a number that's so ungodly huge

510
00:27:39,430 --> 00:27:41,200
我们在宇宙间甚至都没有足够的空间
we don't have enough space in the Universe

511
00:27:41,310 --> 00:27:42,310
将其写下来
even to write it down.

512
00:27:42,430 --> 00:27:44,860
弗里曼：隐形传送人类
Teleporting a human being

513
00:27:44,970 --> 00:27:47,960
远超出我们现在的…能力
is far beyond our capabilities...for now.

514
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:51,200
但史蒂夫和克里斯认为如果可能的话
But Steve and Chris believe if it is possible,

515
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:54,640
量子纠缠将就是其结果
quantum entanglement will be how it's done.

516
00:27:54,750 --> 00:27:57,710
量子力学在实验室里已反复的到了验证
Quantum mechanics has been verified repeatedly in the lab,

517
00:27:57,820 --> 00:28:00,270
在我们的实验室 在世界上许多实验室
our labs and many around the world,

518
00:28:00,390 --> 00:28:01,680
几十年来反复得到了验证
over and over again for decades.

519
00:28:01,790 --> 00:28:04,180
我们不断验证了量子力学
We've continually verified quantum mechanics

520
00:28:04,290 --> 00:28:06,010
是自然界的准确描述
as an accurate description of nature.

521
00:28:06,130 --> 00:28:07,920
门罗：如果我立足于量子力学
lf l am fundamentally quantum mechanical,

522
00:28:08,030 --> 00:28:10,650
隐形传送就更加离不开量子力学了
teleportation better involve quantum mechanics.

523
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,220
我想说如果有别的方法
l would say if there is a different way

524
00:28:12,330 --> 00:28:13,350
来传送物体的话
to teleport objects,

525
00:28:13,470 --> 00:28:15,320
那么不管怎样 就会有另一个理论
then,somehow,there's a different theory

526
00:28:15,440 --> 00:28:16,990
而不是量子力学存在了
than quantum mechanics out there,

527
00:28:17,100 --> 00:28:18,530
我们只是还不知道罢了
and we just don't know it yet.

528
00:28:18,640 --> 00:28:24,630
弗里曼：我们仍然有很长的路要走 在星际旅行
We are still a long way from traveling from star to star

529
00:28:24,750 --> 00:28:27,170
如光束那般速度
as fast as a beam of light.

530
00:28:27,280 --> 00:28:29,500
但若是我们自认为我们对光所理解的一切
But what if everything we thought we understood

531
00:28:29,620 --> 00:28:32,310
实际上是错误的 又当如何呢？
about light is actually wrong?

532
00:28:34,450 --> 00:28:38,790
这位科学家将物理定律来了个彻底颠覆
This scientist is turning the laws of physics upside down.

533
00:28:39,930 --> 00:28:41,520
如果他是对的
And if he's right,

534
00:28:41,630 --> 00:28:44,020
爱因斯坦镇住宇宙的速度极限
the speed limit Einstein slapped on the Universe

535
00:28:44,130 --> 00:28:46,600
有可能得改变了
might have to be changed.

536
00:28:50,700 --> 00:28:53,130
我们生在一个有速度极限的宇宙间 -
We live in a Universe with a speed limit --

537
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:58,430
每小时6.7亿英里
670 million miles per hour.

538
00:28:58,550 --> 00:29:04,100
对 那就是爱因斯坦所说的
Well,that's what Albert Einstein said.

539
00:29:04,220 --> 00:29:07,550
但要是死因斯坦错了呢？
But what if Einstein was wrong?

540
00:29:20,470 --> 00:29:24,600
约翰.韦伯搞大了
John Webb has big plans.

541
00:29:27,870 --> 00:29:31,470
他想改写宇宙规律
He wants to rewrite the laws of the Universe.

542
00:29:31,580 --> 00:29:36,280
一切始于条形码
And it all begins with bar codes.

543
00:29:39,820 --> 00:29:41,510
好 我们来到了超市
Right. So,we're in the supermarket.

544
00:29:41,620 --> 00:29:42,780
我要买一些东西
l'm buying a few things.

545
00:29:42,890 --> 00:29:45,480
这个生菜 举个例子 - 我们知道它是什么
This lettuce,for example -- we know what it is.

546
00:29:45,590 --> 00:29:47,510
生菜上有大量信息
Has a lot of information on the lettuce.

547
00:29:47,630 --> 00:29:49,020
包装上告诉我们 我们能看到那是什么
Tell us on the packet. We can see what it is.

548
00:29:49,130 --> 00:29:52,220
但这里用此种式样来编码
But encoded in this pattern here

549
00:29:52,330 --> 00:29:54,490
激光扫描所采集的
and picked up by the laser that's gonna scan it

550
00:29:54,600 --> 00:29:56,420
是一组信息
is a set of information,

551
00:29:56,540 --> 00:29:59,930
收银员扫描时 激光束
and when the cashier scans it,the laser beam

552
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:03,000
会看到黑线之间的白色缝隙
will look at the white gaps between the black lines,

553
00:30:03,110 --> 00:30:04,900
我们就看到了价格
and we get the price.

554
00:30:05,010 --> 00:30:08,000
所以说有大量信息储存在条形码里
So there's a lot of information stored in the bar code.

555
00:30:12,350 --> 00:30:13,870
弗里曼：约翰是新南威尔士大学的
John is an astrophysicist

556
00:30:13,990 --> 00:30:16,640
天体物理学家
at the University of New South Wales.

557
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:19,980
他所研究的条形码不光是生菜包
The bar codes he studies are not on packages of lettuce,

558
00:30:20,090 --> 00:30:25,290
而且还有遥远星系发出的光
but on light coming from distant galaxies.

559
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,550
如果你将这些星系发来的光线
lf you split the light

560
00:30:27,670 --> 00:30:30,160
分解成彩虹
coming from these galaxies into a rainbow,

561
00:30:30,270 --> 00:30:33,100
你就会发现有某些颜色不见了
you'll discover that certain colors are missing.

562
00:30:35,280 --> 00:30:39,830
这些黑色条纹 叫做光谱线
Those dark bands,called spectral lines,

563
00:30:39,950 --> 00:30:41,770
源自星际气体云的
are caused by the chemical elements

564
00:30:41,880 --> 00:30:43,940
化学元素
in clouds of interstellar gas

565
00:30:44,050 --> 00:30:48,150
吸收了某些频率的星光
absorbing certain frequencies of starlight.

566
00:30:51,090 --> 00:30:54,250
韦伯：你可以从光谱线里认识到大量的东西
You can learn a great deal from spectral lines.

567
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:56,850
根据它们的位置 你可以认出
From their positions,you can identify elements

568
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:59,420
具有特定频率的元素
that have particular frequencies,

569
00:30:59,530 --> 00:31:02,360
所以你能够看到有东西 如氢 氦
so you can see where things like hydrogen or helium

570
00:31:02,470 --> 00:31:03,890
或其它元素出现在哪里
or other elements are present.

571
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:08,200
弗里曼：不过约翰意识到他的星光条形码
But John realized his starlight bar codes

572
00:31:08,310 --> 00:31:11,300
能够告诉他的东西远重要于
could tell him about something much more important

573
00:31:11,410 --> 00:31:12,870
恒星的成分是什么
than what stars were made of.

574
00:31:12,980 --> 00:31:15,700
它能够让他窥测到
lt could give him a glimpse

575
00:31:15,820 --> 00:31:19,470
宇宙中最基本的常量之一 -
into one of the most fundamental constants of the Universe --

576
00:31:19,590 --> 00:31:24,280
电磁力的强度
the strength of the electromagnetic force.

577
00:31:24,390 --> 00:31:27,920
物理学中 所有的力
ln physics,every force

578
00:31:28,030 --> 00:31:30,620
都有粒子携带它
has a particle that carries it.

579
00:31:30,730 --> 00:31:35,790
电磁力的携带者是光 即光子
Electromagnetic force is carried by light,or photons.

580
00:31:35,900 --> 00:31:40,230
电磁力将原子结合在一起
The electromagnetic force keeps atoms glued together

581
00:31:40,340 --> 00:31:42,560
是通过光子连续不断的交换
with a constant exchange of photons

582
00:31:42,680 --> 00:31:47,470
从原子核弹跳到围绕其运行的电子
that bounce from the nucleus to its orbiting electrons.

583
00:31:47,580 --> 00:31:50,370
当光穿越星际星云气体的原子时
When light passes through atoms of interstellar gas,

584
00:31:50,480 --> 00:31:53,440
它能够干扰光子的这种交换
it can interfere with this exchange of photons

585
00:31:53,550 --> 00:31:57,140
把电子敲出轨道
and knock an electron out of its orbit,

586
00:31:57,260 --> 00:31:58,450
但惟有光恰好
but only if the light

587
00:31:58,560 --> 00:32:01,850
具有合适的能量
has exactly the right amount of energy.

588
00:32:01,960 --> 00:32:03,950
所缺失的光的条形码
The bar code of missing light

589
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:08,860
恰好告诉你电磁力的强度
tells you precisely how strong the electromagnetic force is.

590
00:32:08,970 --> 00:32:11,260
韦伯：过去十年左右的时间里
Over the last decade or so,

591
00:32:11,370 --> 00:32:14,160
技术上有了惊人的变化
there's been an amazing change in technology.

592
00:32:14,270 --> 00:32:18,730
人们现在测量遥远的星体
One can now measure the things in distant astronomical objects

593
00:32:18,850 --> 00:32:21,170
其精准远超过地球上以往的测量
more precisely than ever been measured on Earth.

594
00:32:21,280 --> 00:32:23,170
那为研究早期的宇宙
That provides a very strong motivation

595
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:25,910
提供了强大的动力
for studying the early Universe,

596
00:32:26,020 --> 00:32:28,380
因为我们能够度量当时的环境
because we can measure what the conditions were like,

597
00:32:28,490 --> 00:32:30,140
我们能够度量当时的物理学
we can measure what physics was like,

598
00:32:30,260 --> 00:32:31,880
物理学定律
whether the laws of physics

599
00:32:31,990 --> 00:32:34,580
在宇宙偏远地区是否就
there in very remote regions of the Universe

600
00:32:34,690 --> 00:32:36,950
与其在地球上是一模一样的
are the same as they are on Earth.

601
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:38,500
那是相当惊人的
That's pretty amazing.

602
00:32:40,430 --> 00:32:42,560
弗里曼：于是约翰开始搜索苍穹里的
So John began searching the heavens

603
00:32:42,670 --> 00:32:47,360
数十亿光年之外的发光星云
for glowing clouds of gas billions of light-years away.

604
00:32:47,470 --> 00:32:50,700
他利用夏威夷的凯克望远镜
He used the Keck Telescope in Hawaii

605
00:32:50,810 --> 00:32:52,900
来观察北方星空
to look at the northern sky,

606
00:32:53,010 --> 00:32:55,840
利用智利的大望远镜
and the Very Large Telescope in Chile

607
00:32:55,950 --> 00:32:59,650
观察南方星空
which looks out on the southern sky.

608
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:05,750
他看到他的条形码后
And when he looked at his bar codes,

609
00:33:05,860 --> 00:33:10,320
发现了完全出乎意料的东西
he discovered something totally unexpected.

610
00:33:10,430 --> 00:33:13,890
这是气体云看上去的模样
This is what a cloud of gas would look like

611
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,920
如果这就是我们在地球上的实验室里所看到的话
if we were looking at it in the laboratory on Earth.

612
00:33:17,040 --> 00:33:21,900
我们在南半球观察时
When we look in the southern hemisphere,

613
00:33:22,010 --> 00:33:24,160
有些东西略有不同 -
something slightly different --

614
00:33:24,280 --> 00:33:28,240
这条线移向了光谱的红色一端
this line has moved towards the red end of the spectrum,

615
00:33:28,350 --> 00:33:29,470
这里的另一条线
and another line here

616
00:33:29,580 --> 00:33:32,070
则移向了光谱的蓝色一端
has moved towards the blue end of the spectrum.

617
00:33:32,190 --> 00:33:34,680
所以说光谱线的相对距离
So there's a change in the relative spacing

618
00:33:34,790 --> 00:33:36,340
有一个变化
of the spectral lines.

619
00:33:36,460 --> 00:33:39,080
南半球看上去稍有不同
lt looks slightly different in the southern hemisphere.

620
00:33:39,190 --> 00:33:42,320
如果你现在去北半球
lf you now go to the northern hemisphere,

621
00:33:42,430 --> 00:33:45,250
星空方向完全相反
the exact opposite direction on the sky,

622
00:33:45,370 --> 00:33:46,720
此线现在发生了转换
this line has now shifted,

623
00:33:46,830 --> 00:33:50,060
右边的到了左边
instead of to the right,to the left,

624
00:33:50,170 --> 00:33:54,390
而此线从左边转变到了右边
and this line has shifted to the right instead of to the left.

625
00:33:54,510 --> 00:33:57,410
所以形式现在看上去有所不同了
So the patterns now look different.

626
00:34:01,380 --> 00:34:03,870
这有点像你在超市里喝醉了
lt's a little bit as if you're in a supermarket drunk,

627
00:34:03,980 --> 00:34:06,920
看那条形码 形式发生了变化
looking at the bar code,and the pattern has changed.

628
00:34:09,260 --> 00:34:11,210
弗里曼：这些变化的条形码
These shifting bar codes

629
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:13,910
其起因只能是一个情况 -
can only be caused by one thing --

630
00:34:14,030 --> 00:34:17,150
似乎不可能的情况…
something that seems impossible...

631
00:34:17,260 --> 00:34:21,920
物理学的一个基本定律发生了变化
a change in one of the fundamental laws of physics.

632
00:34:22,040 --> 00:34:23,160
我们第一次看到结果时
When we first saw the results,

633
00:34:23,270 --> 00:34:26,190
很难接受它们是正确的
it was hard to accept that they were correct.

634
00:34:26,310 --> 00:34:30,860
我们发现你在一个方向观察星空时
What we found is when you look in one direction on the sky,

635
00:34:30,980 --> 00:34:33,170
电磁力的强度
the strength of the electromagnetic force

636
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:36,500
看上去随着与我们的距离的增加而减弱
appears to decrease with increasing distance from us,

637
00:34:36,620 --> 00:34:39,610
当你在正好相反方向上观察星空时
and when you look in exactly the opposite direction on the sky,

638
00:34:39,720 --> 00:34:41,810
情况恰恰相反
the converse is true.

639
00:34:41,920 --> 00:34:43,780
电磁强度
The strength of electromagnetism

640
00:34:43,890 --> 00:34:47,410
似乎随着你距离的加大而增强
seems to increase as you move to greater distance.

641
00:34:47,530 --> 00:34:50,580
弗里曼：电磁力是
Electromagnetism is the force

642
00:34:50,700 --> 00:34:52,720
由光来传播的力
that is transmitted by light.

643
00:34:52,830 --> 00:34:55,290
因此若是电磁力的强度
So if the strength of electromagnetism

644
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:57,260
不是恒定的话
is not constant,

645
00:34:57,370 --> 00:35:03,100
那就意味着光本身的属性发生了变化
it means that the properties of light itself are changing.

646
00:35:03,210 --> 00:35:04,730
如果约翰.韦伯是正确的
lf John Webb is right,

647
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:09,700
他就推翻了宇宙的一条基本规则
he's overturned one of the basic laws of the Universe.

648
00:35:09,820 --> 00:35:11,370
一旦物理定律
Once the laws of physics

649
00:35:11,480 --> 00:35:13,970
允许在那些方程式里有所变化
are allowed to vary in those equations,

650
00:35:14,090 --> 00:35:16,110
情况就不得不改写了
things have to be rewritten.

651
00:35:16,220 --> 00:35:18,580
所以说要重头再来安排
So it's back to the drawing board

652
00:35:18,690 --> 00:35:20,820
物理学中的某些基本原理
for certain fundamental principles in physics.

653
00:35:27,800 --> 00:35:30,220
弗里曼：难道是爱因斯坦错了？
Could Einstein be wrong?

654
00:35:30,340 --> 00:35:31,830
难道光速在宇宙不同部分
Could the speed of light be different

655
00:35:31,940 --> 00:35:33,630
是不相同的？
in different parts of the cosmos?

656
00:35:33,740 --> 00:35:36,030
在世界的另一头
On the other side of the world,

657
00:35:36,140 --> 00:35:39,200
有一位宇宙学家坚定地回答 没错
one cosmologist is sure the answer is "yes."

658
00:35:39,310 --> 00:35:43,470
他认为光跑得远快于我们的想象
He believes that light can move much faster than we think,

659
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:45,740
也就是 在宇宙中
and that,out there in the Universe,

660
00:35:45,850 --> 00:35:48,910
有高速公路通往外星
there are superhighways to the stars.

661
00:35:54,730 --> 00:35:57,220
早在开启太空时代时
Back at the dawn of the Space Age,

662
00:35:57,330 --> 00:36:01,390
曾全都心系合适的东西
it was all about having the right stuff.

663
00:36:01,500 --> 00:36:05,790
星际旅行第一人同样需要它
The first people who journey to the stars will need it,too.

664
00:36:05,910 --> 00:36:10,200
他们要闯入未知的世界
They will be venturing into the absolute unknown,

665
00:36:10,310 --> 00:36:16,010
或许是首次跑得比光还快
and,perhaps for the first time,traveling faster than light.

666
00:36:17,350 --> 00:36:21,740
理论物理学家乔奥.马古悠
Theoretical physicist Joao Magueijo

667
00:36:21,860 --> 00:36:24,180
认为外太空或许有地方
thinks that there may be regions of outer space

668
00:36:24,290 --> 00:36:27,080
超光速旅行是有可能的
where faster-than-light travel is possible.

669
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:30,080
他开发出这个激进的理论是因为若是没有它
He developed this radical theory because without it,

670
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:33,560
他就无法解释宇宙的模样
he couldn't explain the way the Universe looks.

671
00:36:37,540 --> 00:36:39,160
马古悠：我们观察宇宙时
When we look out into the Universe,

672
00:36:39,270 --> 00:36:41,660
所看到的一切在所有的方向都是一样的
everything looks the same in every direction.

673
00:36:41,770 --> 00:36:43,400
这是个问题
This is a problem,

674
00:36:43,510 --> 00:36:46,570
因为在宇宙问世之后
because during the time the Universe has lived,

675
00:36:46,680 --> 00:36:49,570
其实并没有足够的时间让光的旅行
there really isn't enough time for light to travel around

676
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:53,370
表现出在宇宙中平均分配
for features to be shared around the Universe,

677
00:36:53,490 --> 00:36:56,340
这我们称之为同质化问题
and this we call the homogeneity problem.

678
00:36:56,460 --> 00:36:59,610
弗里曼：同质化问题
The homogeneity problem,

679
00:36:59,730 --> 00:37:02,420
实际上就是所有的星系 所有的物质
the fact that all galaxies and all matter

680
00:37:02,530 --> 00:37:04,580
均匀地分布在整个宇宙间
are evenly spread around the Universe

681
00:37:04,700 --> 00:37:06,350
不管我们朝哪里看
no matter where we look,

682
00:37:06,470 --> 00:37:11,430
这是宇宙学里最大的难题之一
is one of the biggest puzzles in cosmology.

683
00:37:11,540 --> 00:37:16,060
问题在于 科学家并不认为 大爆炸之后
The problem is,scientists don't think there has been enough time

684
00:37:16,180 --> 00:37:20,110
有足够的时间让物质分布得如此均匀
since the Big Bang for matter to spread out so evenly.

685
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:26,720
把大爆炸想象成一个大聚会
lmagine the Big Bang was a big party.

686
00:37:29,690 --> 00:37:31,180
聚会一旦开始
As soon as the party starts,

687
00:37:31,290 --> 00:37:35,780
每个人马上端上一杯同样的酒
everyone instantly has a glass of the same kind of wine.

688
00:37:35,900 --> 00:37:37,720
女侍应怎么会有时间
How would a waitress have time

689
00:37:37,830 --> 00:37:41,160
这么快就为每个人斟上酒的呢？
to serve everyone a glass of wine so quickly?

690
00:37:43,240 --> 00:37:45,130
马古悠：如果她只能以光速移动
lf she can only move at the speed of light,

691
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:49,130
她就没有时间在他们散开之前到达每个人的面前
she won't have time to reach everyone before they disperse,

692
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:51,400
就如大爆炸宇宙模型一般
like the Big-Bang Universe.

693
00:37:51,510 --> 00:37:54,800
弗里曼：大多数科学家解决这个问题
Most scientists solve this problem

694
00:37:54,910 --> 00:37:57,840
所用的理论叫做宇宙膨胀说
with a theory called cosmic inflation.

695
00:37:57,950 --> 00:38:01,610
其概念是一开始时
The idea is that the room stayed small

696
00:38:01,720 --> 00:38:03,780
所呆的房间小得够时间
for longer at the beginning of time,

697
00:38:03,890 --> 00:38:07,380
给女侍应以足够的时间来伺候各位
giving the waitress enough time to serve everyone.

698
00:38:07,490 --> 00:38:10,050
然后 一个神秘的膨胀之力
Then,a mysterious magnifying force

699
00:38:10,160 --> 00:38:12,720
瞬间将房间涨开
inflates the room very rapidly.

700
00:38:12,830 --> 00:38:16,960
人人都得到了饮品 女侍应则汗流浃背了
Everyone gets a drink,and the waitress hardly breaks a sweat.

701
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:22,160
马古悠：宇宙膨胀说称宇宙
Cosmic inflation says the Universe

702
00:38:22,280 --> 00:38:25,070
一开始是难以想象的那么一丁点
started as an unimaginably small pinpoint

703
00:38:25,180 --> 00:38:28,600
集中了宇宙所有的能量
concentrating all the energy of the Universe,

704
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:31,040
而在一开始的万亿万亿
and that in the first trillions of trillions

705
00:38:31,150 --> 00:38:32,640
万亿分之一秒钟之内
of trillions of a second,

706
00:38:32,750 --> 00:38:35,580
宇宙的规模不断地翻番 翻番 翻番
the Universe doubled,doubled,and doubled in size.

707
00:38:35,690 --> 00:38:39,410
最初平滑的那一点
The initial smoothness of that single point

708
00:38:39,530 --> 00:38:44,650
于是扩展到了我们眼下所看到的广袤的空间
then spread to the vast distances we can see nowadays.

709
00:38:44,760 --> 00:38:47,490
弗里曼：但是膨胀说并未得到证实
But inflation is not proven.

710
00:38:47,600 --> 00:38:50,190
它只是个理论
lt's just a theory.

711
00:38:50,300 --> 00:38:53,660
乔奥有了它的替代品 -
And Joao has an alternative to it --

712
00:38:53,770 --> 00:38:55,100
一个刺激的理论
a provocative theory

713
00:38:55,210 --> 00:38:59,040
它有可能将宇宙让我们触手可及了
that might bring the Universe within our reach.

714
00:39:02,150 --> 00:39:04,500
要是 不去改变膨胀的速度 -
What if,instead of changing the rate of expansion,

715
00:39:04,620 --> 00:39:07,410
我们去改变速度的极限 - 光速 又当如何呢？
we change the speed limit -- the speed of light?

716
00:39:07,520 --> 00:39:10,540
那就是我们所谓的光速可变理论
That's what we call the varying speed of light theory.

717
00:39:10,660 --> 00:39:14,580
根据光速可变理论
Under the varying speed of light theory,

718
00:39:14,690 --> 00:39:18,620
我们的女侍应只是在宇宙一开始时
our waitress simply served everyone faster

719
00:39:18,730 --> 00:39:19,890
伺候各位更快些
in the beginning of the Universe

720
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:23,860
于是减缓到了当前的速度
and then slowed down to the current speed,

721
00:39:23,970 --> 00:39:26,430
让我们这些迟来者疑惑她在如此短的时间里
leaving us latecomers wondering how she managed

722
00:39:26,540 --> 00:39:30,430
是如何应付如此大的宇宙的
to serve such a large Universe in such a short time.

723
00:39:30,540 --> 00:39:34,230
弗里曼：乔奥的理论解决了同质化问题
Joao's theory solves the homogeneity problem

724
00:39:34,350 --> 00:39:37,870
和宇宙膨胀说一样有效
just as effectively as cosmic inflation.

725
00:39:37,980 --> 00:39:43,140
不过它也蔑视了爱因斯坦的黄金规则
But it also thumbs its nose at Einstein's golden rule.

726
00:39:43,260 --> 00:39:46,180
这并不完全违背爱因斯坦的原则
This does not exactly contradict Einstein's principle

727
00:39:46,290 --> 00:39:48,850
即光速是速度的极限
that the speed of light is the speed limit.

728
00:39:48,960 --> 00:39:50,950
我们只是说速度极限的改变
We're only saying that the speed limit

729
00:39:51,060 --> 00:39:54,020
贯穿了宇宙的一生
changed throughout the life of the Universe.

730
00:39:54,130 --> 00:39:57,690
弗里曼：乔奥的理论意味着
And Joao's theory means there might be a way

731
00:39:57,800 --> 00:40:00,690
可能有办法去打破今天的宇宙速度极限
to break today's cosmic speed limit,

732
00:40:00,810 --> 00:40:04,100
因为可能有途径穿越空间
because there could be pathways through space

733
00:40:04,210 --> 00:40:07,230
在那里光速依然保持得更快些
where the speed of light remains faster.

734
00:40:07,350 --> 00:40:11,370
这些途径被称为宇宙弦
These pathways are called cosmic strings.

735
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:13,910
马古悠：根据可变光速理论
Under the varying speed of light theory,

736
00:40:14,020 --> 00:40:16,910
光在宇宙开始时要跑得更快些
light traveled faster in the beginning of the Universe,

737
00:40:17,020 --> 00:40:19,910
宇宙弦可能就是那些地区
and cosmic strings could be regions

738
00:40:20,030 --> 00:40:23,020
在那里这种更高速度极限依然行之有效
where this higher speed limit is still in force.

739
00:40:23,130 --> 00:40:27,390
弗里曼：其概念就是在宇宙的
The idea is that,in the first moments

740
00:40:27,500 --> 00:40:28,560
最初一刻
of the Universe,

741
00:40:28,670 --> 00:40:32,160
细小的破碎就已经形成于时空间了
tiny fractures formed in space-time.

742
00:40:32,270 --> 00:40:34,760
从那时起 这些破碎
Since then,these fractures

743
00:40:34,870 --> 00:40:37,930
随着宇宙中其他东西一起扩张
expanded along with everything else in the cosmos

744
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:41,500
直到现在几十亿光年之久
and are now billions of light-years long.

745
00:40:41,610 --> 00:40:46,010
宇宙弦可能充当高速通道
Cosmic strings might serve as high-speed lines

746
00:40:46,120 --> 00:40:47,270
直达那些你慢慢爬行
cutting across regions

747
00:40:47,390 --> 00:40:49,980
所无法抵达的地区
where you would otherwise be moving at a crawl.

748
00:40:53,660 --> 00:40:55,280
你可能觉得宇宙弦
You could think of cosmic strings

749
00:40:55,390 --> 00:40:56,860
就像是伦敦的地铁…
like the Tube in London...

750
00:41:01,070 --> 00:41:04,590
…在那里 地面上 有速度限制
...where,on the surface,there is a speed limit,

751
00:41:04,700 --> 00:41:08,500
但是显然在地下并无限制
but obviously down there there isn't one.

752
00:41:08,610 --> 00:41:11,600
弗里曼：在地表 爱因斯坦的限制就是法律
On the surface,Einstein's limit is the law.

753
00:41:11,710 --> 00:41:15,170
地铁就是宇宙弦 -
The Tube below is the cosmic string --

754
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:18,540
穿城的快速通道
a faster way across town.

755
00:41:18,650 --> 00:41:20,810
如果你装备有一艘飞船
lf you could fit a spacecraft

756
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:23,140
能进入宇宙弦周围所创造出来的
into the corridor of high speed limit

757
00:41:23,260 --> 00:41:25,010
更高速度极限的通道
created around the cosmic string,

758
00:41:25,120 --> 00:41:28,060
快速穿越宇宙将会成为可能
fast travel throughout the Universe would become possible.

759
00:41:31,360 --> 00:41:34,350
弗里曼：宇宙弦尚未被发现
Cosmic strings have yet to be found,

760
00:41:34,470 --> 00:41:38,730
可变光速依然还是一个理论
and the variation in the speed of light is still just a theory.

761
00:41:41,310 --> 00:41:43,430
但是逐渐并坚定不移地
But slowly and steadily,

762
00:41:43,540 --> 00:41:47,600
科学家们 如乔奥.马古悠和约翰.韦伯
scientists like Joao Magueijo and John Webb

763
00:41:47,710 --> 00:41:51,170
正在逐渐瓦解爱因斯坦的宇宙速度极限
are chipping away at Einstein's cosmic speed limit.

764
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,510
卡罗尔：你开始怀疑
You begin to wonder,

765
00:41:52,620 --> 00:41:54,840
若是它在宇宙间从此地至那地发生变化
what if it changes from place to place in the Universe,

766
00:41:54,950 --> 00:41:57,540
或许其曾处于宇宙历史的不同的早期
or maybe it was different early on in the Universe's history,

767
00:41:57,660 --> 00:41:59,450
如果光速是变化的
and if the speed of light is changing,

768
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:01,480
那么我们有对物理学的大量认识
then a lot of what we think about physics

769
00:42:01,590 --> 00:42:04,340
在宇宙早期至今也会有所不同
could be different in the early Universe to today.

770
00:42:04,460 --> 00:42:05,460
弗里曼：世界各地
Around the world,

771
00:42:05,570 --> 00:42:08,150
科学家们正在测试新的技术
scientists are testing new technologies

772
00:42:08,270 --> 00:42:10,820
深入探寻物理学的核心
and probing deep into the heart of physics

773
00:42:10,940 --> 00:42:13,760
来揭秘宇宙的新的规律
to uncover new laws of the Universe,

774
00:42:13,870 --> 00:42:18,470
以找到方法让我们脱离我们的地球村
to find a way for us to escape our island Earth.

775
00:42:20,510 --> 00:42:25,610
我们要成为宇宙公民依然路途漫漫
We are still a long way from becoming citizens of the cosmos.

776
00:42:25,720 --> 00:42:30,410
外星仍然几乎是遥不可及
The stars remain almost unimaginably far away.

777
00:42:30,520 --> 00:42:33,050
但不管科学接下来何去何从
But wherever science goes next,

778
00:42:33,160 --> 00:42:38,520
我们探索这个终极疆域的希望将永不泯灭
our hopes to explore this final frontier will never be dimmed.

779
00:42:38,630 --> 00:42:42,290
有朝一日 我们将抵达那里
And,one day,we will reach it,

780
00:42:42,400 --> 00:42:47,570
因为人类敢想敢为
because what man can imagine,man can do.

781
00:42:49,350 --> 00:42:51,590
-- 感谢观赏 --

